#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:9
msgid "Speeding up pytest startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:12
msgid "Preface: the migration to pytest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:14
msgid ""
"Last year, after 17 years of :mod:`unittest`, I started adopting pytest in "
"psutil (see :gh:`2446`). The two advantages I cared about most were plain "
"``assert`` statements and `pytest-xdist <https://pypi.org/project/pytest-"
"xdist/>`__'s free parallelism. Tests still inherit from :class:`unittest."
"TestCase` and there's no ``conftest.py`` or fixture use (rationale in :pr:"
"`2456`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:21
msgid ""
"What I want to focus on here is one of pytest's most frustrating aspects: "
"slow startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:25
msgid "pytest invocation is slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:27
msgid ""
"To measure pytest's startup time, let's run a very `simple test <https://"
"github.com/giampaolo/psutil/blob/265fcf94a5da4260beb514653a2124915bf2a4f2/"
"psutil/tests/test_misc.py#L232-L236>`__ where execution time itself is "
"negligible:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:31
msgid ""
"$ time python3 -m pytest psutil/tests/test_misc.py::TestMisc::test_version\n"
"1 passed in 0.05s\n"
"real    0m0,427s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:37
msgid ""
"Almost half a second, which is excessive for something I run repeatedly "
"during development. For comparison, the same test under :mod:`unittest`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:40
msgid ""
"$ time python3 -m unittest psutil.tests.test_misc.TestMisc.test_version\n"
"Ran 1 test in 0.000s\n"
"real    0m0,204s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:46
msgid "Roughly twice as fast. Why?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:49
msgid "Where is time being spent?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:51
msgid ""
"A significant portion of pytest's overhead comes from import time, and "
"there's not much one can do about it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:54
msgid ""
"$ time python3 -c \"import pytest\"\n"
"real    0m0,151s\n"
"\n"
"$ time python3 -c \"import unittest\"\n"
"real    0m0,065s\n"
"\n"
"$ time python3 -c \"import psutil\"\n"
"real    0m0,056s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:66
msgid "Disable plugin auto loading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:68
msgid ""
"After some research, I discovered that pytest automatically loads all "
"plugins installed on the system, even if they aren't used. Here's how to "
"list them (output is cut):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:72
msgid ""
"$ pytest --trace-config --collect-only\n"
"...\n"
"active plugins:\n"
"    ...\n"
"    setupplan           : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"setupplan.py\n"
"    stepwise            : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"stepwise.py\n"
"    warnings            : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"warnings.py\n"
"    logging             : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"logging.py\n"
"    reports             : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"reports.py\n"
"    python_path         : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"python_path.py\n"
"    unraisableexception : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"unraisableexception.py\n"
"    threadexception     : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"threadexception.py\n"
"    faulthandler        : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/_pytest/"
"faulthandler.py\n"
"    instafail           : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/"
"pytest_instafail.py\n"
"    anyio               : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/anyio/"
"pytest_plugin.py\n"
"    pytest_cov          : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pytest_cov/"
"plugin.py\n"
"    subtests            : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/"
"pytest_subtests/plugin.py\n"
"    xdist               : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/xdist/plugin."
"py\n"
"    xdist.looponfail    : ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/xdist/"
"looponfail.py\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:95
msgid ""
"It turns out ``PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD`` environment variable can be "
"used to disable them. By running ``PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 pytest --"
"trace-config --collect-only`` again I can see that the following plugins "
"disappeared:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:100
msgid ""
"anyio\n"
"pytest_cov\n"
"pytest_instafail\n"
"pytest_subtests\n"
"xdist\n"
"xdist.looponfail"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:109
msgid "Now let's run the test again with ``PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:111
msgid ""
"$ time PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 python3 -m pytest psutil/tests/"
"test_misc.py::TestMisc::test_version\n"
"1 passed in 0.05s\n"
"real    0m0,285s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:117
msgid ""
"We went from 0.427s to 0.285s, a ~40% improvement. Not bad. We now need to "
"selectively enable only the plugins we actually use, via ``-p``. psutil uses "
"``pytest-instafail`` and ``pytest-subtests`` (we'll deal with ``pytest-"
"xdist`` later):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:122
msgid ""
"$ time PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 python3 -m pytest -p instafail -p "
"subtests ...\n"
"real    0m0,320s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:127
msgid ""
"Time went back up to 0.320s. Quite a slowdown, but still better than the "
"original 0.427s. Adding ``pytest-xdist``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:130
msgid ""
"$ time PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 python3 -m pytest -p instafail -p "
"subtests -p xdist ...\n"
"real    0m0,369s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:135
msgid ""
"0.369s. Not much, but still a pity to pay the price when NOT running tests "
"in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:139
msgid "Handling pytest-xdist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:141
msgid ""
"If we disable ``pytest-xdist`` psutil tests still run, but we get a warning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:143
msgid ""
"psutil/tests/test_testutils.py:367\n"
"  ~/svn/psutil/psutil/tests/test_testutils.py:367: PytestUnknownMarkWarning: "
"Unknown pytest.mark.xdist_group - is this a typo?  You can register custom "
"marks to avoid this warning - for details, see https://docs.pytest.org/en/"
"stable/how-to/mark.html\n"
"    @pytest.mark.xdist_group(name=\"serial\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:149
msgid ""
"This warning appears for methods that are intended to run serially, those "
"decorated with ``@pytest.mark.xdist_group(name=\"serial\")``. However, since "
"``pytest-xdist`` is now disabled, the decorator no longer exists. To address "
"this, I implemented the following solution in ``psutil/tests/__init__.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:154
msgid ""
"import pytest, functools\n"
"\n"
"PYTEST_PARALLEL = \"PYTEST_XDIST_WORKER\" in os.environ  # True if running "
"parallel tests\n"
"\n"
"if not PYTEST_PARALLEL:\n"
"    def fake_xdist_group(*_args, **_kwargs):\n"
"        \"\"\"Mimics `@pytest.mark.xdist_group` decorator. No-op: it just\n"
"        calls the test method or return the decorated class.\"\"\"\n"
"        def wrapper(obj):\n"
"            @functools.wraps(obj)\n"
"            def inner(*args, **kwargs):\n"
"                return obj(*args, **kwargs)\n"
"\n"
"            return obj if isinstance(obj, type) else inner\n"
"\n"
"        return wrapper\n"
"\n"
"    pytest.mark.xdist_group = fake_xdist_group  # monkey patch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:175
msgid ""
"With this in place the warning disappears when running tests serially. To "
"run tests in parallel, we'll manually enable ``xdist``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:178
msgid "$ python3 -m pytest -p xdist -n auto --dist loadgroup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:183
msgid "Optimizing test collection time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:185
msgid ""
"By default, pytest searches the entire directory for tests, adding "
"unnecessary overhead. In ``pyproject.toml`` you can tell pytest where test "
"files are located, and only to consider ``test_*.py`` files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:189
msgid ""
"[tool.pytest.ini_options]\n"
"testpaths = [\"psutil/tests/\"]\n"
"python_files = [\"test_*.py\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:195
msgid "Collection time dropped from 0.20s to 0.17s, another ~0.03s shaved off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:198
msgid "Putting it all together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/speedup-pytest-startup.rst:200
msgid ""
"With these small optimizations, I managed to reduce ``pytest`` startup time "
"by ~0.12 seconds, bringing it down from 0.42 seconds. While this improvement "
"is insignificant for full test runs, it makes a noticeable difference (~28% "
"faster) when repeatedly running individual tests from the command line, "
"which is something I do frequently during development. Final result is "
"visible in :pr:`2538`."
msgstr ""

